{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01BtXF8SZsqJW6qWX3WiuqdH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a clear picture:\n\n1. **TASK**: 5-slot structured prompt about amplitude-scaling measured blast vibration records for TSF dynamic response review\n2. **KB**: \n   - EMPTY-KB.md - no content\n   - T1.compile.research.md - about blast vibration standards/criteria (not directly relevant to amplitude scaling)\n   - T3.compile.research.md - about EMD/EEMD filtering of blast records (partially relevant for context)\n3. **Constraints**: \n   - Not spectral matching\n   - Not physics-based blast source synthesis\n   - No claim of direct pore-pressure prediction from acceleration alone\n4. **Next steps**: The knowledge base doesn't have dedicated material on amplitude scaling of blast records for scenario studies, so I need to search the literature. I'm looking for work on ground motion record scaling from earthquake engineering, blast record scaling approaches, how scaling compares to spectral matching, and applications to tailings storage facility dynamic analysis.\n\n5. **Key gaps to address**: I need external sources to support the amplitude-scaling approach itself, clarify what properties it preserves and what it doesn't, justify the assumptions behind independent component-peak scaling, distinguish this method from spectral matching and synthetic waveforms, and find defensible language for describing scenario demand histories.\n\nNow I'm searching Zotero and the web for literature on ground motion scaling, blast vibration scaling, and related methodologies.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5333,"cache_read_input_tokens":49166,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5333,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":27,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics